    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-016.png\" width=\"909\" height=\"1271\" alt=\"Question 3: Disposal of subsidiary \nYou are the finance manager of Bolt Shoes Ltd (Bolt), a UK-based company. Bolt has \none subsidiary, Edwards Trainers Ltd (Edwards) and you are preparing the \nconsolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 20X3 in \naccordance with IFRS Accounting Standards. The main business activity of the group \ndoes not include investing in assets or providing finance. \n \nYou have prepared all the journals except the disposal journal. Bolt acquired 80% of \nEdwards’ 100,000 shares several years ago and goodwill of £100,000 was \nrecognised. Bolt sold its entire shareholding in Edwards on 31 December 20X3 for \n£2,000,000. Proceeds were recognised as Dr Cash and cash equivalents and Cr \nRevenue. \n \nAt 31 December 20X3 goodwill had been impaired by £20,000.  \n \nThe equity of Edwards at 31 December 20X3 is: \n \n \n30 December 20X3 \n \n£’000 \nShare capital \n100 \nShare premium \n50 \nRetained earnings \n2,200 \nTotal equity \n2,350 \n \n \nRequired \n1. Prepare, showing all workings, the disposal journal for the year ended 31 \nDecember 20X3. \n2. Assume Bolt only sold 10,000 shares in Edwards on 31 December 20X3 and \nproceeds were £250k. Proceeds were recognised as Dr Cash and cash \nequivalents and Cr Revenue. Prepare, showing all workings, the disposal \njournal for the year ended 31 December 20X3.\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-017.png\" width=\"909\" height=\"1273\" alt=\"Question 3: Disposal of subsidiary \nRequirement 1 \n \nCarrying amount of goodwill = £100,000 - £20,000 = £80,000 \n \n \n£000 \nProceeds on disposal \n2,000 \n \n \nNet assets of sub at disposal date (100%) \n(2,350) \nNCI at disposal date (20% x £2,350k) \n470 \nGoodwill at disposal date (£100k – 20k) \n(80) \n \n \nGain on disposal \n40 \n \n \n \n£000 \n£000 \nDr Revenue \n2,000 \n \nDr SOFP - NCI \n470 \n \n     Cr Goodwill \n \n80 \n     Cr Net assets disposed \n \n2,350 \n     Cr SPL – gain on disposal \n \n40 \nBeing disposal of Edwards subsidiary \n \n \n \nRequirement 2 \n \n \n£000 \nProceeds on disposal \n250 \nRecognition of increase in NCI (10% x £2,350k) \n(235) \nGain on disposal \n15 \n \n \n \n£000 \n£000 \nDr Revenue \n250 \n \n     Cr SOFP - NCI \n \n235 \n     Cr Retained earnings \n \n15 \nBeing partial disposal of Edwards subsidiary\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "searchText": "Question 3: Disposal of subsidiary \nYou are the finance manager of Bolt Shoes Ltd (Bolt), a UK-based company. Bolt has \none subsidiary, Edwards Trainers Ltd (Edwards) and you are preparing the \nconsolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 20X3 in \naccordance with IFRS Accounting Standards. The main business activity of the group \ndoes not include investing in assets or providing finance. \n \nYou have prepared all the journals except the disposal journal. Bolt acquired 80% of \nEdwards’ 100,000 shares several years ago and goodwill of £100,000 was \nrecognised. Bolt sold its entire shareholding in Edwards on 31 December 20X3 for \n£2,000,000. Proceeds were recognised as Dr Cash and cash equivalents and Cr \nRevenue. \n \nAt 31 December 20X3 goodwill had been impaired by £20,000.  \n \nThe equity of Edwards at 31 December 20X3 is: \n \n \n30 December 20X3 \n \n£’000 \nShare capital \n100 \nShare premium \n50 \nRetained earnings \n2,200 \nTotal equity \n2,350 \n \n \nRequired \n1. Prepare, showing all workings, the disposal journal for the year ended 31 \nDecember 20X3. \n2. Assume Bolt only sold 10,000 shares in Edwards on 31 December 20X3 and \nproceeds were £250k. Proceeds were recognised as Dr Cash and cash \nequivalents and Cr Revenue. Prepare, showing all workings, the disposal \njournal for the year ended 31 December 20X3.",
